---
title: Milestone review
---
flowchart TD
    classDef human fill:#fff3cd,stroke:#8a6d3b,color:#000
    classDef role fill:#d9edf7,stroke:#31708f,color:#000
    classDef channel fill:#dff0d8,stroke:#3c763d,color:#000
    classDef stop fill:#eeeeee,stroke:#777,color:#000

    START(["Every sub-milestone under the parent<br/>stands at ✅ Done — the Task writer set<br/>each one as it moved off it, which required<br/>the human accepting every subtask"]):::human
    MR["Milestone Reviewer — whole-milestone scope.<br/>Functionality and gaps, never code style:<br/>fmt and clippy are the style gate"]:::role

    WHICH{"Reviewed: line on the<br/>milestone's roadmap entry?"}

    C1["1. The roadmap entry:<br/>does the code satisfy the Solution and<br/>every line of Done-when?<br/>Not 'did each subtask land'"]
    C2["2. Cross-cutting invariants across the<br/>milestone as a whole — multi-step protocols<br/>whose individual steps are each correct<br/>are the classic failure"]
    C3["3. Documentation truth:<br/>every touched .MD still describes the code,<br/>every referenced ADR exists, decisions are<br/>recorded somewhere durable"]
    C4["4. Status: roadmap markers match reality,<br/>sub-milestone ids referenced from code<br/>and .MD files resolve to real headings"]
    C5["5. Forward dependencies: did this milestone<br/>leave work a later one now silently<br/>depends on?"]
    C6["6. Deferred items: anything the Coder or<br/>the human's review put off is written down,<br/>not in someone's head"]
    REPORT["All six reported in the reply, 'nothing'<br/>included — a check that found nothing and<br/>a check never run look identical otherwise"]

    VERIFY["Verification pass — scope is exactly the<br/>repairs: did each gating entry's fix land and<br/>do what the entry asked, and what did those<br/>commits change? No re-audit of the milestone"]

    SPLIT{"Each finding:<br/>does it violate a named Done-when line,<br/>the Solution, or a docs/agent-guide.md invariant?"}
    GATE["Gating — entry in .claude/problems.md<br/>naming that line. The parent stays 🚧"]:::channel
    NONGATE["Non-gating — entry in .claude/problems.md<br/>like any other problem. Triaged and<br/>scheduled by Importance; the milestone<br/>passes with it still open"]:::channel
    FWD["Write a forward dependency into the<br/>later milestone's docs/ROADMAP.md entry"]

    REVLINE["Append one Reviewed: line to the milestone<br/>entry — date, which pass, gating and<br/>non-gating P- numbers. The only fact that<br/>survives to the next pass"]:::channel
    LOOP(["Task writer routes fixes by Owner:<br/>the assigned role works each subtask<br/>— see agent-flow-problem-lifecycle.mmd"]):::stop

    VERDICT{"Anything gating open?"}
    DONE["Set the parent milestone to ✅ Done in<br/>docs/ROADMAP.md and delete its Reviewed:<br/>lines in the same edit. Only this role sets a<br/>parent: the functionality was reviewed whole<br/>and works and nothing gating stands — not<br/>that the queue is empty"]
    HUMAN["Human reviews and commits"]:::human
    NEXT(["Next milestone<br/>— see agent-flow-milestone-planning.mmd"]):::stop

    START --> MR --> WHICH
    WHICH -- "no — pass 1" --> C1 --> C2 --> C3 --> C4 --> C5 --> C6 --> REPORT --> SPLIT
    WHICH -- "yes — repair landed" --> VERIFY --> SPLIT
    SPLIT -- "yes" --> GATE --> VERDICT
    SPLIT -- "no" --> NONGATE --> VERDICT
    SPLIT -- "forward dependency" --> FWD --> VERDICT
    VERDICT -- "yes" --> REVLINE --> LOOP
    LOOP -. "milestone comes back" .-> MR
    VERDICT -- "no" --> DONE --> HUMAN --> NEXT
